format = arf1.0
language = EN

%help
@title
Format of Sequencing Data
@paragraph
10X single-cell sequencing data are stored in FASTQ format, which is the standard output format for Illumina sequencing platform. See attached Figure 3 for examples of data. This file consists of four action units: the first line begins with '@', followed by the sequence description; The second line is the sequence; The third line begins with a '+', which may or may not be followed by the sequence description; The fourth line is the base quality value of the second line sequence, and the two lines are correspond one by one. An example is shown as the following:

\verbatim
\@A00228:279:HFWFVDMXX:1:1101:8486:1000 2:N:0:NCATTACT
NACAAAGTCCCCCCCATAATACAGGGGGAGCCACTTGGGCAGGAGGCAGGGAGGGGTCCATTCCCCCTGGTGGGGCTGGTGGGGAGCTG
+
\#FFFFFFFFFFFFFFF:FFFFFFF:FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF:FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF:FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF
\end

@title
Data Delivery
@paragraph
For some big raw data, suach as raw sequencing fastq、alignment bam and experession gem，and some big analysis results，suach as gem of tissue、rds of cell cluster，are delivered by a Portable Hard Disk(PHD) or Cloud Disk . The directory structure is consistent with this report;
All standard analysis results have been shown in this report, and all tables and figures (including pdf) have been put in the corresponding directory which will not be delivered again.
The detailed directory and files are shown as the following:
\verbatim
    Directory                                       Content            Files            Deliver method
|-- IDBiotech_result
|-- QC.xls                                    QC report   
|-- Mapping.xls                               QC report
|-- Cell.xls                                  QC report
|   |-- Sample1                              Sample Name                        
|   |   |-- 01.Data_report                    Data report
|   |   |   |-- LibraryID1                                            Library of Sample         This report  
|   |   |       |-- *xls                                                report         This report      
|   |   |-- 02.Normalize                      Data Normalize
|   |   |   |-- *pdf                          Analysis result pdf       This report                             
|   |   |   |-- *png                          Analysis result png       This report
|   |   |-- 03.HvgPCA                         High variableFeatures                This report
|   |   |   |-- *pdf                                            Analysis result png        This report
|   |   |   |-- *png                                            Analysis result png         This report
|   |   |-- 04.Decontamination                        Data Cleaning
|   |   |   |-- *pdf                                            Analysis result png        This report
|   |   |   |-- *png                                            Analysis result png         This report
